check 1
# Binding a skill hotkey with real input: the right skill list is opened (held click on the
# button), the pointer goes onto the Throw icon, F1 is pressed twice. The 1.14d client sends
# C->S 0x51 (bind; then clear and bind again); the server sends no S->C 0x7B for it
# (0x7B comes only at the join of a save that holds hotkeys). pc1-data.md Step 4 [rc-link-2].
# Spec: specs/tools/scenario-diff.md §3 (input).
name net-hotkey-bind-ama
save ScnAma --class ama --expansion
seed 1234
ticks 80
seconds 300
channels packets
input orig frame 40; hold 660 570 2; frame 50; move 660 500; frame 56; key 112; frame 64; key 112
